IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Railway Transfer Ordinance 1918 (Singapore) -- what vested in the Chief Secretary, Federation of Malaya (s 2), additional
-- Crown land for the railway (s 3), taking back land no longer used for the railway and what is paid for it (ss 4, 5), the causeway
-- and the works for it (ss 6, 7), and the narrow right to compensation for land injured by the works (ss 8, 9).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SRTO1918.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The latest amending instruments its
-- Legislative History lists are of 1959 (Ordinances 62 and 72 of 1959 and G.N. Nos. S (N.S.) 177-179/1959); the last revised edition
-- listed before 2020 is the 1985 Revised Edition (operation 30 March 1987). The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is
-- one line out of step with the body; this file follows the body's numbering (s 1 short title ... s 10 private Act).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0254 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. For a private person the answer is mostly ss 8 and 9: who may claim compensation for the causeway works.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the recitals (the $4,136,000 consideration is quoted but not computed with), s 1 (short title), s 10 (the Ordinance is
-- deemed a private Act for the Registration of Deeds Act 1988; stated in a comment only), the roadways and footways in s 6(b) beyond a
-- single rule, and anything about whether any land is still vested today -- the deposit does not say.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the other naive rows (the writing-l4-rules skill
-- was not loadable in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Railway Transfer Ordinance 1918 -- railway lands`

§§ `2 -- what vested in the Chief Secretary`

-- s 2: "The railway known as the Singapore Railway whereof the terminal stations are situated at Pasir Panjang and at Woodlands",
-- together with (a) "all lands delineated and coloured pink on a plan deposited in the Colonial Secretary's office dated 18 March
-- 1913 ... described thereon as 'Singapore Railway Lands'"; (b) lines, bridges, stations, offices, quarters, warehouses, workshops,
-- plant, wharves "and other buildings and works constructed or used for the purposes of or in connection with" the railway; (c)
-- ships, wagon-ferry-boats, engines, coaches, wagons and other rolling stock "which were on the 31 December 1912, the property of the
-- Colony and used or maintained for the purposes of" the railway; and (d) "the cable across the Johore Straits which was laid for
-- railway purposes exclusively" -- "are hereby vested, free from encumbrances, in the Chief Secretary, Federation of Malaya,
-- absolutely".
DECLARE Thing IS ONE OF
    `land coloured pink on the 1913 plan`
    `land not shown pink on the 1913 plan`
    `a station or workshop used for the railway`
    `a wharf used for the railway`
    `an engine or wagon`
    `a wagon-ferry-boat`
    `the cable across the Johore Straits`

GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing, `Colony property on 31 December 1912 and used for the railway` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `laid exclusively for railway purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing vested under section 2` IF
    CONSIDER `the thing`
    WHEN `land coloured pink on the 1913 plan` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `land not shown pink on the 1913 plan` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a station or workshop used for the railway` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a wharf used for the railway` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an engine or wagon` THEN `Colony property on 31 December 1912 and used for the railway`
    WHEN `a wagon-ferry-boat` THEN `Colony property on 31 December 1912 and used for the railway`
    WHEN `the cable across the Johore Straits` THEN `laid exclusively for railway purposes`

§§ `3 -- additional Crown land for the railway`

-- s 3(1): if the Government of the Federation of Malaya require "additional Crown land" for the railway "and such requirement is
-- approved either in whole or in part by the Yang di-Pertuan Negara, such land shall be surveyed and demarcated to the satisfaction
-- of the Collector of Land Revenue". (2) the Registrar of Deeds "shall, on receipt of an order in that behalf under the hand of the
-- Minister, make an entry". (3) "Upon the making of any such entry ... the land ... shall vest free from encumbrances ... absolutely".
-- (4) "No payment, other than for the cost of survey and demarcation, shall be required".
GIVEN `received the Minister's order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must make the entry` IF `received the Minister's order`

GIVEN `the Registrar has made the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the additional land has vested under section 3` IF `the Registrar has made the entry`

GIVEN `cost of survey and demarcation` IS A NUMBER, `market value of the land` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the payment required for section 3 land` IS `cost of survey and demarcation`

§§ `4, 5 -- taking back land not used for the railway`

-- s 4(1): land vested under s 2 or s 3 which "is not used and will not be required to be used or ceases to be used" for the railway
-- "may, if the Yang di-Pertuan Negara so directs, be resumed on 6 months' notice under the hand of the Minister". (2) "On the
-- expiration of the term of such notice the Yang di-Pertuan Negara may authorise the Collector of Land Revenue to enter and take
-- possession".
-- s 5(1): other land "acquired by the Government of the Federation of Malaya for the purposes of" the railway, if likewise unused,
-- "together with any buildings thereon may be purchased by the Yang di-Pertuan Negara on 6 months' notice under the hand of the
-- Minister". (2) "On the expiration of the term of such notice THE MINISTER may authorise the Collector".
-- So under s 4 it is the Yang di-Pertuan Negara who authorises entry; under s 5 it is the Minister.
DECLARE Origin IS ONE OF
    `vested by section 2`
    `vested by section 3`
    `acquired otherwise for the railway`
    `not railway land`

DECLARE Resumption HAS
    `origin` IS AN Origin
    `still used or required for the railway` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Yang di-Pertuan Negara wants it back` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months since the Minister's notice` IS A NUMBER
    `entry authorised by the Yang di-Pertuan Negara` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry authorised by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the resumption` IS A Resumption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the right person authorised entry` IF
    CONSIDER `the resumption`'s `origin`
    WHEN `vested by section 2` THEN `the resumption`'s `entry authorised by the Yang di-Pertuan Negara`
    WHEN `vested by section 3` THEN `the resumption`'s `entry authorised by the Yang di-Pertuan Negara`
    WHEN `acquired otherwise for the railway` THEN `the resumption`'s `entry authorised by the Minister`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the resumption` IS A Resumption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Collector may take possession` IF
        (NOT `the resumption`'s `origin` EQUALS `not railway land`)
    AND (NOT `the resumption`'s `still used or required for the railway`)
    AND `the resumption`'s `the Yang di-Pertuan Negara wants it back`
    AND `the resumption`'s `months since the Minister's notice` AT LEAST 6
    AND `the right person authorised entry` `the resumption`

-- s 4(3): for s 2 land, (a) there is paid "such sum ... as was paid by the Government of the Federated Malay States ... for the
-- purchase of the land so resumed together with such sum as represents the value, at the date of resumption, of all buildings
-- erected by or on behalf of" that Government; (b) if nothing was paid for the land, nothing is paid for it, but the buildings are
-- still paid for. (4) for s 3 land, "nothing shall be paid ... for such land", only the buildings. s 5(3): for other land the price
-- of land and buildings is agreed, or if not agreed "ascertained by a person to be selected by the Yang di-Pertuan Negara".
-- The survey cost paid under s 3(4) is not returned: s 4(4) pays for buildings only (inference from silence).
GIVEN `origin of the land` IS AN Origin, `price paid for the land under the transfer` IS A NUMBER,
      `value of buildings at resumption` IS A NUMBER, `agreed or ascertained price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the sum paid on taking back` IS
    CONSIDER `origin of the land`
    WHEN `vested by section 2` THEN `price paid for the land under the transfer` PLUS `value of buildings at resumption`
    WHEN `vested by section 3` THEN `value of buildings at resumption`
    WHEN `acquired otherwise for the railway` THEN `agreed or ascertained price`
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 4(5), 5(3): if the two Governments "do not agree", the valuation (s 4) or price (s 5) goes to "a person, to be selected by the
-- Yang di-Pertuan Negara, who shall be a Member or Associate Member of the Institution of Civil Engineers, or a Fellow or Associate of
-- the Royal Institution of British Architects". s 4(6), 5(4): that person's decision "shall be final and binding on both parties".
DECLARE Qualification IS ONE OF
    `Member of the Institution of Civil Engineers`
    `Associate Member of the Institution of Civil Engineers`
    `Fellow of the Royal Institution of British Architects`
    `Associate of the Royal Institution of British Architects`
    `a valuer licensed in Singapore`
    `a Singapore professional engineer`

GIVEN `the qualification` IS A Qualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the qualification is one the Act names` IF
    CONSIDER `the qualification`
    WHEN `a valuer licensed in Singapore` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Singapore professional engineer` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the Governments agree` IS A BOOLEAN, `the qualification` IS A Qualification,
      `selected by the Yang di-Pertuan Negara` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may decide the valuation` IF
        (NOT `the Governments agree`)
    AND `selected by the Yang di-Pertuan Negara`
    AND `the qualification is one the Act names` `the qualification`

§§ `6, 7 -- the causeway and the works for it`

-- s 6: the Government of the Federated Malay States "may, with the approval of the Legislative Council -- (a) construct ... a causeway
-- or embankment, in accordance with a plan to be approved by the Legislative Council, suitable for the passage of railway traffic;
-- (b) construct ... a railway ... and such roadways and footways as to the Government of the Colony seem expedient".
GIVEN `the Legislative Council approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `the plan was approved by the Legislative Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the causeway may be built` IF `the Legislative Council approved` AND `the plan was approved by the Legislative Council`

GIVEN `the causeway may lawfully be built` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Colony Government thinks it expedient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a roadway may be built on the causeway` IF `the causeway may lawfully be built` AND `the Colony Government thinks it expedient`

-- s 7: for preliminary examination of the bed of the Straits, and operations incidental to construction, protection, maintenance and
-- use, the Government "or any person authorised by it in that behalf may take borings and construct piers and abutments ...
-- notwithstanding that obstruction is thereby caused to the passage of ships, boats or other craft".
GIVEN `for examining the Straits bed or building, protecting, maintaining or using the causeway` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `by the Government or a person it authorised` IS A BOOLEAN, `it obstructs ships or boats` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operation is authorised by section 7` IF
    `for examining the Straits bed or building, protecting, maintaining or using the causeway` AND `by the Government or a person it authorised`

§§ `8, 9 -- compensation for the works`

-- s 8: "Except as in section 9 provided, no person shall claim, and no action or proceeding shall be brought ... to recover, any
-- compensation in respect of any lands or of any interest therein which have been injuriously affected by anything done in pursuance
-- of this Ordinance or in respect of any obstruction to the flow of water or to the passage of ships or boats ... or any alteration in
-- the tides".
-- s 9: "There shall be a right of compensation in respect of any lands or of any interest therein which has been injuriously affected
-- ..., if the damage ... is -- (a) damage caused by reason of what has been authorised by this Ordinance; (b) damage arising from the
-- execution of the works authorised by this Ordinance and not by their subsequent use; and (c) damage arising from that which would,
-- if done without the authority of this Ordinance, have given rise to a cause of action; and where the compensation is claimed in
-- respect of any interference with a public or private right, is -- (d) damage arising from a physical interference with a right ...
-- which gives an additional market value to such property apart from the uses to which any particular owner or occupier might put it."
-- So a person with no land or interest in land (a boatman, a ferry operator) has no claim, and damage from the trains' later use is
-- outside s 9(b). Who pays, how much, and before which body is not said in the Ordinance.
DECLARE Claim HAS
    `land or an interest in land was injuriously affected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by what the Ordinance authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from executing the works, not their later use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would have been actionable without the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `claimed for interference with a public or private right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a physical interference with a right that adds market value to the property` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a right to compensation` IF
        `the claim`'s `land or an interest in land was injuriously affected`
    AND `the claim`'s `caused by what the Ordinance authorised`
    AND `the claim`'s `arose from executing the works, not their later use`
    AND `the claim`'s `would have been actionable without the Ordinance`
    AND (    (NOT `the claim`'s `claimed for interference with a public or private right`)
         OR  `the claim`'s `a physical interference with a right that adds market value to the property`)

-- s 10: "For the purposes of the Registration of Deeds Act 1988 this Ordinance shall be deemed to be a private Act." Not encoded.
